#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:250
msgid ""
"† 双極子にはピークがないため、原子の座標から求めた対称伸縮のスペクトル（ :numref:`fig-co2-spectra` と :numref"
":`fig-co2-spectra-bomd` の右）のピークの位置です。BOMDでも、双極子のスペクトルにν₁のピークは現れませんでした。"
msgstr ""
"† Since there is no peak in the dipole spectrum, these are the peak "
"positions in the symmetric stretching spectra derived from the atomic "
"coordinates (right-hand panels of :numref:`fig-co2-spectra` and :numref"
":`fig-co2-spectra-bomd`). The ν₁ peak was absent from the BOMD dipole "
"spectrum as well."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:252
msgid ""
"\\* ν₁は2ν₂とほぼ同じエネルギーにあるため、両者が混ざり合い（フェルミ共鳴 [8]_ ）、ラマンスペクトルでは1285 cm⁻¹と1388"
" cm⁻¹の2本に分かれて観測されます。1333 cm⁻¹は、混ざり合いがない場合の推定値です。"
msgstr ""
"\\* Because ν₁ and 2ν₂ are nearly equal in energy, they mix (Fermi "
"resonance [8]_) and appear as two separate lines at 1285 cm⁻¹ and 1388 "
"cm⁻¹ in the Raman spectrum. The value 1333 cm⁻¹ is the estimate without "
"mixing."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:254
msgid ""
"MDのピークの位置は、計算時間で決まる分解能（約42 cm⁻¹）の精度で読み取った値です。\\ BOMDの時間刻み0.5 "
"fsでは、時間積分の誤差のためにν₃が約0.2 %高めに出ますが、分解能よりずっと小さい差です。"
msgstr ""
"We read the MD peak positions to the resolution set by the run duration "
"(about 42 cm⁻¹). \\ With the 0.5 fs BOMD time step, the time integration "
"error shifts ν₃ upward by about 0.2 %, but this shift is much smaller "
"than the resolution."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:257
msgid "この表から、次のことが読み取れます。"
msgstr "The table shows the following trends."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:259
msgid ""
"**CPMDの振動数は、すべてのモードでBOMDより低くなっています。** 低下の割合は、ν₁で4.3 %、ν₂で約3 %、ν₃で6.4 "
"%です。2つの計算は初期条件が同じで、違いは電子の扱いと時間刻みです。時間刻みによる差は上で述べたとおり小さい（ν₃で約0.2 "
"%）ので、この低下はCPMDの仮想質量の影響です。CPMDでは、電子の波動関数が仮想的な質量を持つために原子の動きに少し遅れてついていき、原子が実際より重くなったように振る舞います。このため振動数が低めに出ることが知られています"
" [5]_ 。"
msgstr ""
"**CPMD gives lower frequencies than BOMD for every mode.** The "
"frequencies are 4.3 % lower for ν₁, about 3 % for ν₂, and 6.4 % for ν₃. "
"The two calculations start from the same initial conditions and differ "
"only in the treatment of the electrons and the time step. The time step "
"has only a small effect, as noted above (about 0.2 % for ν₃), so this "
"decrease results from the fictitious mass in CPMD. Because the electronic"
" wavefunctions have a fictitious mass, they lag slightly behind the "
"motion of the atoms, making the atoms behave as though they were heavier."
" This effect is known to lower the frequencies [5]_."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:260
msgid ""
"**BOMDの振動数は、実験の調和振動数より0.7〜3.1 %低くなっています。** "
"原子核を古典的に扱う低温のMDで得られる振動数は、ほぼ調和振動数に相当します。そのため、非調和性を含む実験の基本振動数ではなく、実験から求めた調和振動数（表の右端の列）と比べるのが適切です。BOMDのν₃（2348"
" cm⁻¹）は基本振動数（2349 "
"cm⁻¹）とほぼ一致していますが、これは計算の誤差と非調和性の効果がたまたま打ち消し合ったものです。調和振動数との差（ν₁で3.1 %、ν₂の "
":math:`x` 成分で1.8 %、 :math:`y` 成分で0.7 %、ν₃で2.0 "
"%）が、PBE、擬ポテンシャル、格子などの今回の計算条件による誤差です。"
msgstr ""
"**The BOMD frequencies are 0.7–3.1 % below the experimental harmonic "
"frequencies.** At low temperatures, MD with classical nuclei gives "
"frequencies that are close to the harmonic frequencies. The appropriate "
"comparison is therefore with the harmonic frequencies derived from "
"experiment (rightmost column), since the experimental fundamental "
"frequencies include anharmonicity. The BOMD value for ν₃ (2348 cm⁻¹) "
"nearly matches the fundamental frequency (2349 cm⁻¹), but only because "
"the calculation error and the effect of anharmonicity happen to cancel. "
"The differences from the harmonic frequencies (3.1 % for ν₁, 1.8 % for "
"the :math:`x` component and 0.7 % for the :math:`y` component of ν₂, and "
"2.0 % for ν₃) reflect the error due to the calculation conditions used "
"here, including PBE, the pseudopotentials, and the real-space grid."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:261
msgid ""
"**静的計算は、ν₁とν₃ではBOMDとほぼ一致しています。** 変角振動ν₂だけは、静的計算がBOMDより約4 %低くなっています。 "
":numref:`tab-co2-harmonic` "
"の後の注で述べたとおり、静的計算の変角の値は、原子と格子の相対位置によるエネルギーの揺らぎのために不確かです。"
msgstr ""
"**The static calculations agree closely with BOMD for ν₁ and ν₃.** Only "
"for the bending mode ν₂ is the static frequency about 4 % below BOMD. As "
"discussed in the note after :numref:`tab-co2-harmonic`, the static "
"bending frequency is uncertain because the energy varies with the "
"positions of the atoms relative to the real-space grid."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:263
msgid ""
"CPMDの結果だけを静的計算と比べると、変角振動の振動数はほぼ一致するので、仮想質量の影響は伸縮振動だけに現れるように見えます。\\ "
"BOMDと直接比べると、実際にはすべてのモードの振動数が下がっていたことが分かります。"
msgstr ""
"Comparing only CPMD with the static calculations gives nearly the same "
"bending frequency, so the fictitious mass appears to affect only the "
"stretching modes. \\ A direct comparison with BOMD shows that CPMD in "
"fact lowers the frequencies of all the modes."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:269
msgid "吸収強度"
msgstr "Absorption Intensity"

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:296
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-co2-spectra` および :numref:`fig-co2-spectra-bomd` "
"の双極子スペクトルの強度は、そのままでは実際の赤外吸収強度に対応しません。\\ 各ピークの面積は、その成分の双極子の揺らぎの分散に比例します。\\"
" 変角振動の基準座標を :math:`Q` とすると、分散は :math:`(\\partial\\mu_x/\\partial "
"Q)^2\\langle Q^2\\rangle` で、\\ 分子固有の性質である双極子の変化率 "
":math:`\\partial\\mu/\\partial Q` の2乗と、そのモードの基準座標の2乗平均 :math:`\\langle "
"Q^2\\rangle` の積です。"
msgstr ""
"The intensities of the dipole spectra in :numref:`fig-co2-spectra` and "
":numref:`fig-co2-spectra-bomd` do not directly correspond to actual "
"infrared absorption intensities. \\ The area under each peak is "
"proportional to the variance of the fluctuations of that dipole "
"component. \\ If :math:`Q` is the normal coordinate for bending, the "
"variance is :math:`(\\partial\\mu_x/\\partial Q)^2\\langle Q^2\\rangle`. "
"\\ The dipole derivative :math:`\\partial\\mu/\\partial Q` is an "
"intrinsic molecular property. The variance is the product of the square "
"of this derivative and the mean square of the normal coordinate "
":math:`\\langle Q^2\\rangle` for the mode."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:301
msgid ""
"今回の計算は、孤立した分子1個の短いNVE計算なので、各モードの振幅はランダムに与えた初速度によるエネルギーの配分に依存します。\\ 実際、 "
":math:`x` 方向と :math:`y` 方向の変角振動は、振幅が3.7倍違い、 :math:`C_x` と :math:`C_y` "
"のピークの高さは約14倍違います。\\ 十分に長い熱平衡の計算や多数の計算の平均で、各モードに同じエネルギーが入っていれば、 "
":math:`\\omega^2 C(\\omega)` のバンドの面積は赤外強度に比例するのですが、\\ "
"今回の計算はその条件を満たしていません。"
msgstr ""
"These short NVE runs follow a single isolated molecule, so the amplitude "
"of each mode depends on how the random initial velocities distribute "
"energy. \\ In fact, bending along :math:`x` and :math:`y` differs in "
"amplitude by a factor of 3.7, and the peak heights of :math:`C_x` and "
":math:`C_y` differ by a factor of about 14. \\ If each mode receives the "
"same energy in a sufficiently long run at thermal equilibrium or in an "
"average over many runs, the band area in :math:`\\omega^2 C(\\omega)` is "
"proportional to IR intensity. \\ The present calculation, however, does "
"not meet this condition."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:309
msgid ""
"そこで、振幅によらない量として、双極子の変化率 :math:`\\partial\\mu/\\partial Q` "
"をMDシミュレーションの軌跡から直接求めます。\\ 各時刻の原子座標から質量で重みをつけた基準座標 :math:`Q` "
"を求め、双極子との間で線形回帰を行いました。\\ 分子軸の傾きが小さい最初の400 fsを使っています。\\ 赤外強度（吸収バンドの積分強度）は"
msgstr ""
"We therefore obtain the amplitude-independent dipole derivative "
":math:`\\partial\\mu/\\partial Q` directly from the MD trajectory. \\ We "
"computed the mass-weighted normal coordinate :math:`Q` from the atomic "
"coordinates at each time and performed a linear regression of the dipole "
"moment against it. \\ We used the first 400 fs, when the molecular axis "
"was tilted only slightly. \\ The IR intensity (the integrated intensity "
"of the absorption band) is given by"

