#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:453
msgid ""
"CPMDでは、対称伸縮振動の振幅は600 fsまでに3分の1に減り、その間に変角振動の振幅は5倍に増えています。\\ "
"対称伸縮振動のエネルギーが、変角振動に移っていったのです。\\ 最適化構造から始めた計算（青）では、変角振動の振幅はほぼ一定でした。"
msgstr ""
"In CPMD, the symmetric stretching amplitude fell to one-third of its "
"initial value by 600 fs, while the bending amplitude increased fivefold "
"over the same time. \\ Energy passed from the symmetric stretching mode "
"to the bending mode. \\ The bending amplitude was nearly constant in the "
"run starting from the optimized structure (blue)."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:457
msgid ""
"BOMDでも変角振動の振幅は増えますが、500 fsごろに約3倍になったところで頭打ちになり、その後は減り始めます。\\ "
"対称伸縮振動の振幅も、2割ほど減ったところで増加に転じます。\\ "
"エネルギーは一方的に移るのではなく、2つの振動の間を行き来しているように見えます。"
msgstr ""
"In BOMD, the bending amplitude also increased, but it peaked at about "
"three times its initial value around 500 fs and then began to fall. \\ "
"The symmetric stretching amplitude, in turn, began to rise after falling "
"by about 20 %. \\ Energy appears to move back and forth between the two "
"modes, with no one-way transfer."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:461
msgid ""
"CPMDの振動数は、ν₁が1218 cm⁻¹、ν₂が約610 cm⁻¹で、ν₁ ≈ 2ν₂の関係がほぼ成り立っています。\\ 変角の座標の2乗 "
":math:`Q_2^2` は2ν₂の振動数で変化するので、ポテンシャルに :math:`Q_1 Q_2^2` "
"の項（非調和項）があると、ν₁の振動と共鳴してエネルギーを効率よくやり取りできます。\\ これは、 :numref:`tab-co2-freq` "
"の脚注（\\*）で触れたフェルミ共鳴と同じ組み合わせです。\\ "
"フェルミは、この非調和項による2つの準位の混ざり合いで、CO₂のラマンスペクトルが2本に分かれることを説明しました [8]_ 。\\ "
"ここで見ているのは、同じ非調和項によるモード間のエネルギーのやり取りを、古典力学で追ったものです。"
msgstr ""
"The CPMD frequencies are 1218 cm⁻¹ for ν₁ and about 610 cm⁻¹ for ν₂, so "
"ν₁ ≈ 2ν₂. \\ The squared bending coordinate :math:`Q_2^2` varies at "
"frequency 2ν₂. If the potential contains a :math:`Q_1 Q_2^2` term (an "
"anharmonic term), this variation can resonate with the oscillation at ν₁ "
"and allow efficient energy exchange. \\ This is the same pairing of modes"
" as in the Fermi resonance mentioned in the footnote (\\*) to :numref"
":`tab-co2-freq`. \\ Fermi explained the two lines in the CO₂ Raman "
"spectrum by the mixing of two levels through this anharmonic term [8]_. "
"\\ What we see here is the exchange of energy between modes through the "
"same anharmonic term, followed with classical mechanics."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:467
msgid "実際のCO₂でも、ν₁（混ざり合いがない場合の推定値1333 cm⁻¹）と2ν₂（2×667 cm⁻¹）はほぼ等しくなっています。"
msgstr ""
"In actual CO₂, ν₁ (estimated at 1333 cm⁻¹ in the absence of mixing) and "
"2ν₂ (2×667 cm⁻¹) are also nearly equal."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:469
msgid ""
"BOMDでは、ν₁が1319 cm⁻¹、ν₂が約651 cm⁻¹で、2ν₂はν₁より約15 cm⁻¹低くなっています。\\ この差は分解能（約42"
" cm⁻¹）より小さいので目安ですが、共鳴から少しずれているとエネルギーは行き来するだけになるので、BOMDの振る舞いと整合します。\\ "
"CPMDでは、仮想質量による振動数の低下に加え、電子の仮想的な運動エネルギーが最大1.3×10⁻⁴ "
"Haまで増えていて、振動のエネルギーの一部が電子の仮想的な運動に移っています（平均温度がBOMDより低いのもこのためと考えられます）。\\ "
"どちらがエネルギーの移り方の違いの原因なのかは切り分けていませんが、CPMDで見えたエネルギーの移動の速さや量を、実際の分子の性質として読むことはできません。"
msgstr ""
"In BOMD, ν₁ is 1319 cm⁻¹ and ν₂ is about 651 cm⁻¹, so 2ν₂ is about 15 "
"cm⁻¹ below ν₁. \\ This difference is only an estimate because it is "
"smaller than the resolution (about 42 cm⁻¹). However, slightly off "
"resonance the energy merely moves back and forth, consistent with the "
"behavior in BOMD. \\ In CPMD, in addition to the lower frequencies due to"
" the fictitious mass, the fictitious electronic kinetic energy rose to as"
" much as 1.3×10⁻⁴ Ha, with some of the vibrational energy transferred to "
"the fictitious motion of the electrons (which may also explain the lower "
"average temperature than in BOMD). \\ We did not isolate which of these "
"two effects accounts for the difference in energy transfer, but the rate "
"and amount of transfer seen in CPMD cannot be taken as properties of the "
"actual molecule."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:475
msgid "この数値実験から分かること"
msgstr "What the Numerical Experiment Shows"

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:477
msgid "外部電場をかけない第一原理MDでも、双極子モーメントの揺らぎから、赤外活性な振動（変角ν₂と逆対称伸縮ν₃）の振動数を取り出せました。"
msgstr ""
"Even without an applied external electric field, we obtained the "
"frequencies of the IR-active vibrations (bending ν₂ and antisymmetric "
"stretching ν₃) from fluctuations in the dipole moment in first-principles"
" MD."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:478
msgid "対称伸縮振動ν₁は、原子が振動していても双極子には現れず、赤外不活性であることを直接確かめられました。"
msgstr ""
"We directly confirmed that symmetric stretching ν₁ is IR inactive. It "
"produces no dipole signal even when the atoms vibrate."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:479
msgid ""
"CPMDでは、同じ初期条件のBOMDより、すべてのモードの振動数が3〜6 %低く出ました。BOMDの振動数は実験の調和振動数より0.7〜3.1 "
"%低く、これがPBEと今回の計算条件による誤差です。実験と比べるときは、両者を分けて考える必要があります。"
msgstr ""
"With the same initial conditions, CPMD gave frequencies 3–6 % lower than "
"BOMD for every mode. The BOMD frequencies were 0.7–3.1 % below the "
"experimental harmonic frequencies, reflecting the error from PBE and the "
"calculation conditions used here. A comparison with experiment must "
"distinguish these two shifts."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:480
msgid ""
"双極子のパワースペクトルのピークの高さは、各モードに入ったエネルギーで変わるので、赤外強度を表しません。振幅によらない双極子の変化率 "
":math:`\\partial\\mu/\\partial Q` "
"をMDの軌跡から求めると、BOMDの赤外強度はν₃、ν₂とも実験値より小さめでしたが、両者の比（約13）は実験（約12）に近い値でした。"
msgstr ""
"The peak heights in the power spectra of the dipole moment change with "
"the energy that goes into each mode, so they do not represent IR "
"intensities. When we obtained the amplitude-independent dipole derivative"
" :math:`\\partial\\mu/\\partial Q` from the MD trajectory, the BOMD IR "
"intensities for both ν₃ and ν₂ were somewhat lower than the experimental "
"values, but their ratio (about 13) was close to the experimental ratio "
"(about 12)."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:481
msgid "対称伸縮振動を大きく励起すると、CPMDでもBOMDでも、差音・結合音が双極子に現れました。フェルミ共鳴によるエネルギーの移動も見えましたが、その大きさはCPMDとBOMDで大きく異なりました。"
msgstr ""
"Strong excitation of the symmetric stretching mode produced difference "
"bands and combination bands in the dipole spectrum in both CPMD and BOMD."
" We also saw energy transfer due to Fermi resonance, but the amount "
"transferred differed substantially between CPMD and BOMD."

#: ../../co2_ir/ir_spectrum.rst:483
msgid ""
"今回の計算は、原子核を古典的に扱った、3原子の分子1個・800 fsの計算です。\\ "
"零点振動などの量子効果は含まれず、熱平衡の統計平均でもありません。\\ 得られた振動数や強度は、この条件での計算結果として読んでください。"
msgstr ""
"These calculations followed one three-atom molecule for 800 fs and "
"treated the nuclei classically. \\ They omit quantum effects such as "
"zero-point vibration and do not provide a statistical average at thermal "
"equilibrium. \\ Interpret the frequencies and intensities as results "
"under these specific conditions."

